ata/2023554/000162828025050180/0001628280-25-050180-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-08-14","form":"8-K","codes":["2.02","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000119312525180782/0001193125-25-180782-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-05-07","form":"8-K","codes":["2.02","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000202355425000021/0002023554-25-000021-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-03-11","form":"8-K","codes":["5.02"],"events":[{"label":"Director or officer departure or appointment","kind":"people","tone":"warn"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000202355425000007/0002023554-25-000007-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-02-24","form":"8-K","codes":["1.01","2.03","3.03","5.01","5.02","5.03","5.05","8.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Material agreement entered","kind":"deal","tone":"good"},{"label":"Took on a material obligation","kind":"finance","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Holder rights modified","kind":"finance","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Change in control","kind":"governance","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Director or officer departure or appointment","kind":"people","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Fiscal year or bylaws amended","kind":"governance","tone":"blue"},{"label":"Other material event","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000119312525033433/0001193125-25-033433-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-02-14","form":"8-K","codes":["3.03","5.03","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Holder rights modified","kind":"finance","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Fiscal year or bylaws amended","kind":"governance","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000119312525027285/0001193125-25-027285-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-02-03","form":"8-K","codes":["8.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Other material event","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000119312525019298/0001193125-25-019298-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[],"summary":{"sentences":["Sandisk Corp files with the SEC under \"Computer Storage Devices\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 1 year.","It reported $13.0bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 251.0% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 78.4%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($357.0m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 251.0% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $6.0bn in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 4 of the last 5 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Gross margin of 78.4% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Gross margin expanded from 22.5% to 78.4% against the same quarter a year earlier - the company is keeping more of what it sells, not buying growth with discounts.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $357.0m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828025050698/0001628280-25-050698-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-25-050698"},{"text":"Net cash of $3.7bn against total assets of $17.1bn - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 93.1% across 5 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 8.3% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.5% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000136324926000056/0001363249-26-000056-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 70.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.7,"consecutive":2,"current":0.784,"current_display":"78.4%","threshold_display":"70.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 126.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":1.26,"consecutive":2,"current":2.51,"current_display":"251.0%","threshold_display":"126.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 15.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.15,"consecutive":1,"current":0.083,"current_display":"8.3%","threshold_display":"15.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.0,"consecutive":1,"current":0.0,"current_display":"0.00","threshold_display":"1.00","fired":false,"rationale":"Past this point creditors, not shareholders, decide what happens next.","editable":true},{"id":"going_concern","kind":"event","label":"Going-concern doubt appears in any filing","metric":"going_concern","comparison":"is_true","threshold":true,"current":false,"current_display":"not present","fired":false,"rationale":"The auditors saying the company may not survive the year is not a signal to interpret. It is the exit.","editable":false}],"team":[{"raw_name":"Goeckeler David","role":"Officer","title_filed":"Chairman and CEO","shares":509903.0,"sold_in_window":0.0,"bought_in_window":0.0,"last_filing":"2026-05-27","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0002023554","confidence":"filed","prior_companies":[]},{"raw_name":"Visoso Luis Felipe","role":"Officer","title_filed":"EVP and Chief Financial Office","shares":165058.0,"sold_in_window":0.0,"bought_in_window":0.0,"last_filing":"2026-05-22","source